# - {rsp_files: '5, ALL single-matrix .rsp v01. ZERO .rsp2 exist for this burst. Per D2 this must NOT be reported as a NO-RSP2 failure
#     - scripts/10::find_rsp accepts .rsp'}
# - {d1_theta_check: RUN - mandatory here because every response is single-matrix AND the burst triggered a Fermi ARR slew (GCN 12449)}
# - {d1_result: 'max Delta-theta across the stamped source window = 0.19 deg (n7 and n9); D1 threshold is 4 deg, so ALL FOUR RESPONSES
#     ARE VALID over the window we fit'}
# - {arr_slew: 'GCN 12449 verbatim - this burst was ''bright enough to result in a Fermi spacecraft autonomous rapid repoint (ARR) maneuver''.
#     Slew onset measured from poshist at t approx +52 to +55 s, i.e. AFTER the source window closes at +15 s'}
# - {slew_over_src_window_deg: 0.644}
# - {slew_over_bkgpos_window_deg: 10.67}
# - {FLAG_BACKGROUND_NONSTATIONARY: 'The POST background interval +25..+135 s straddles the ARR slew - the spacecraft boresight moves
#     10.67 deg across it (n6 20.43 -> 12.25 deg, b1 55.93 -> 63.46 deg). About +25..+52 s is attitude-stable; +52..+135 s is not. A polynomial
#     background fit over this span assumes a rate-stationary detector orientation, which is false here because Earth-limb and albedo
#     geometry track attitude. This does NOT invalidate any response - it is a background-model risk that propagates into every block.
#     Recommended Step 5/6 sensitivity check - refit the background with the post window truncated to +25..+50 s and compare block-level
#     parameters. NOTE this is a flag on an ALREADY-APPROVED human selection, raised for the record, not an instruction to change it'}
# - {d4_note: 'T90_START = +0.256 s, T90 = 11.07 +/- 0.41 s (GBM catalog, 50-300 keV), so the T90 span +0.26..+11.33 s sits inside the
#     stamped window -1.0/+15.0 s. GCN 12449 reports ''one main peak'' - no pre-trigger episode. Yu+2019 and Shao+2017 both open their
#     source interval at -5 s and report no earlier emission'}
# - {verdict: PASS_WITH_FLAG}
# - {verdict_detail: 'Responses PASS the D1 off-axis test, which is the correct test for single-matrix DRMs. File manifest is complete
